{{Quote|I've made myself a little roost at the top of an old communications tower. These towers used to serve a purpose here. They were used to guide the few visitors who came to Lothal to the spaceports. That was before the Empire. Now the Empire controls most of the traffic in and out, and it has left these old towers empty. That's how Imperial progress works. Throw away the old. I won't let this one go to waste, though.|Ezra Bridger|<ref name="A New Hero">''[[Star Wars Rebels: A New Hero]]''</ref>}}
'''LothalNet comm tower E-272''', also known as '''Ezra's Roost''' or '''Lothal Transmitter Tower''', was a disused [[LothalNet]] [[comm tower]] located in the plains outside [[Lothal]]'s [[Capital City]]. About five [[Standard year|years]] before the [[Battle of Yavin]], the young orphan [[Ezra Bridger]] used it as a hideout while living as an orphan before joining the [[Spectres]] rebel group. Later during the early [[New Republic Era]], Bridger's friend [[Sabine Wren]] lived in the tower with her [[loth-cat]] [[Murley]].

==Description==
[[File:Ezras tower.png|thumb|left|The tower in the Imperial Era.]]
The LothalNet comm tower E-272,<ref name="Journal" /> also simply known as the Lothal Transmitter Tower,<ref name="DB">{{Databank|lothal-transmitter-tower|Lothal Transmitter Tower}}</ref> was located on the [[planet]] [[Lothal]], standing solitary in the [[grass]]lands outside of [[Capital City|Lothal City]],<ref name="Spark" /> specifically in Grid Q6 in the [[Western Zone]].<ref name="Journal" /> A two-lane highway led away from the city in the direction of the tower, but terminated in a u-turn around halfway to the tower without having connected to anywhere. The foot of the tower was surrounded by a small grey-colored area followed by a pattern of lines in the form of rings surrounding it intercepted by wider lines pointing away. The tower itself consisted of a tall spike narrowing before getting wider at the top where it had three large antennas&mdash;two horizontally and one vertically.<ref name="Spark" /> The tower was accessed through a room at the base with a [[turbolift]] leading to several empty rooms encircled by a balcony,<ref name="USW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> at the top in between the antennas. During the [[Imperial Era]], the tower also had multiple additional antennas further down,<ref name="Spark" /> which had been removed at the time of the [[New Republic Era]], as did the line patterns around the base.<ref name="Part One">{{Ahsoka|Part One: Master and Apprentice}}</ref>

The tower was at one point used by [[LothalNet]] but eventually was abandoned and used by the [[human]] [[Ezra Bridger]] as a hideout,<ref name="Journal" /> and was thus referred to as Ezra's Roost. Bridger used the room at the base to store his [[speeder]]s, while using one of the upper rooms for his bunk and storing his possessions<ref name="USW" /> like his collection of stolen [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Armor|helmets]]<ref name="The Visual Guide">''[[Star Wars Rebels: The Visual Guide]]''</ref> and decorated it with [[graffiti]].<ref name="Spark" /> From the balcony Bridger had an expansive view<ref name="USW" /> on the surrounding grasslands and the Capital City.<ref name="Spark" /> When [[Sabine Wren]] later took over Bridger's room, she added various possessions and decorated the room with various new colorful graffiti and doodles<ref name="Part One" /> and stored multiple storage containers and [[Sabine's speeder bike|her speeder bike]] outside the base of the tower and a brightly-painted barrel on the balcony.<ref name="Part Two">{{Ahsoka|Part Two: Toil and Trouble}}</ref>

==History==
===Imperial Era===
After the comm tower was abandoned by LothalNet, Bridger used the tower as a hideout while living as an orphan.<ref name="Journal" /> In [[5 BBY]],<ref name="Property date">{{RebelsDate|S4}}</ref> was walking in the grasslands outside the tower and investigated a shot down [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter]].<ref name="Property of Ezra Bridger">{{Rebels|Property of Ezra Bridger}}</ref> Later that year,<ref name="Spark date">{{RebelsDate|101}}</ref> Bridger stood at the balcony of the tower when he saw an [[Imperial I-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial I''-class Star Destroyer]] passing overhead. He then drove with his [[614-AvA speeder bike]] heading to the Capital City. In the City, [[Mission in Capital City|Bridger stole]] another [[speeder bike]] with crates from the rebel group known as the [[Spectres]], who themselves had only stolen it from the Imperials moments earlier. Followed by the Spectres members [[Kanan Jarrus]] and [[Garazeb Orrelios]] and two [[Imperial combat driver]]s, Bridger tried to return to his hideout. He managed to loose his pursuers on the highway, but his speeder was shot down by a TIE fighter before he was saved by the Spectres's [[starship]], the ''[[Ghost]]''. After having helped the Spectres [[Mission to free Wookiee prisoners|free a group of prisoners]] on [[Spice mine K76|Kessel]], Bridger returned to his hideout at the tower. Jarrus followed Bridger inside to talk to him and persuade him to join their team and be trained by him in [[the Force]]. Afterwards the Spectres continued to wait in the ''Ghost'' outside the tower and Bridger ultimately his old hideout and decided to join them.<ref name="Spark" /> Bridger later returned to the tower on [[Empire Day]]<ref name="Empire Day">{{Rebels|Empire Day (episode)}}</ref> of that year<ref name="EmpireDay date">{{RebelsDate|108}}</ref> to retrieve the [[keycard]] to his [[Bridger household|old family home]] and heard the voices of his [[Mira Bridger|mother]] and [[Ephraim Bridger|father]].<ref name="Empire Day" />

[[2 BBY|Two years]]<ref name="ZH Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of "[[Zero Hour]]" to [[2 BBY]].</ref> after it had been abandoned by Bridger, it was used by the rogue [[Imperial Security Bureau]] [[agent]] [[Alexsandr Kallus]] to secretly contact the Rebels using the codename [[Fulcrum]]. After learning that [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]] was aware of the planned rebel strike on Lothal, Kallus tried to use a [[transmitter]] to warn the [[Phoenix Cell]]. However, Thrawn jammed the signals and captured Kallus following a fight. Using the trajectories of Kallus' Fulcrum transmissions and [[General]] [[Jan Dodonna]]'s [[Massassi Group]], Thrawn was able to find the [[Chopper Base|hidden rebel base]] in the [[Atollon system]].<ref name="Zero Hour">{{Rebels|Zero Hour}}</ref> When the [[Spectres]] [[Theft of the TIE Defender Elite|returned]] to Lothal<ref name="Flight of the Defender" /> in [[1 BBY]],<ref name="FotD Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of "[[Flight of the Defender]]" to [[1 BBY]].</ref> [[Kanan Jarrus]], [[Hera Syndulla]], and [[C1-10P|Chopper]] conducted a long-distance reconnaissance of Lothal City from the tower. They discovered preparations at the [[Imperial Armory Complex]] indicating that the Empire planned to mass-produce the newly-developed [[TIE/D Defender Elite]].<ref name="Flight of the Defender" /> After Syndulla had been captured by the Empire, the tower's convenient view of the capital was used for recon in preparation for her [[Rescue of Hera Syndulla (Lothal)|rescue]].<ref name="Jedi Night">{{Rebels|Jedi Night}}</ref>

===New Republic Era===
[[File:Sabines feeds Murley - Ahsoka Ep1.png|thumb|Sabine Wren [[Foodstuff|feeds]] her loth-cat Murley in her room.|400x400px]]
After the [[liberation of Lothal]], the tower was eventually restored,<ref name="Farewell">{{Rebels|Family Reunion &ndash; and Farewell}}</ref> and [[Sabine Wren]] lived there together with her [[loth-cat]] [[Murley]] to watch over Lothal as a promise to her missing friend Bridger.<ref name="Part One" /> In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{AhsokaSeriesDate}}</ref> Wren watched an old recording from Bridger on her [[Sabine's holoprojector|imagecaster]], where Bridger reminded Wren of her mission. Wren then gazed the sky and saw the [[T-6 1974|T-6 shuttle]] of her former master [[Ahsoka Tano]] and her [[X-wing starfighter|X-wing]] escort approach Lothal City from the tower's balcony. The evening after, Wren researched [[Arcana Star Map|the star map]] that Tano had [[Mission to Arcana|recovered]] from [[Arcana]]. However, shortly after she managed to open it, the [[Force-sensitive]] [[human]] [[Shin Hati]] and several [[HK-87 assassin droid]]s attacked the tower, [[Duel on Lothal|dueling]] and stabbing Sabine before escaping with the map sought by [[Morgan Elsbeth]].<ref name="Part One" /> The following days while Wren recovered in the [[Lothal Hospital]], Tano visited the comm tower where she [[Psychometry|sensed]] the duel through the Force. She then greeted Murley on the balcony and investigated Wren's room and was repelled the ambush of a HK-87 assassin droid, who had hidden on the ceiling. After recovering, Wren returned to her home to assemble [[Sabine Wren's armor|her armor]] and joined her former master on her [[quest to find Ezra Bridger]].<ref name="Part Two" />

==Behind the scenes==
The LothalNet comm tower E-272 first appeared in the ''[[Rise of the Rebels]]'' chapter book,<ref name="Rise of the Rebels">''[[Rise of the Rebels]]''</ref> released on [[August 5]], [[2014]],<ref name="Disney">{{Disney|subdomain=books|url=book/star-wars-rebels-rise-of-the-rebels|text=Star Wars Rebels: Rise of the Rebels|nolive=1}}</ref> which adapted the short "[[Property of Ezra Bridger]]" from the animated series ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'',<ref name="Property of Ezra Bridger" /> released the following month.<ref name="Insider 156">{{InsiderCite|156|Star Wars Rebels Recounted|''Star Wars Rebels'' Recounted}}</ref> Early concept art of Bridger's room in the tower was done by [[Chris Glenn]].<ref name="Spark concept">{{SW|url=series/spark-of-rebellion-concept-art-gallery|text="Spark of Rebellion" Concept Art Gallery}}</ref> The tower was later recreated in live-action for the [[2023]] TV series ''[[Star Wars: Ahsoka]]''.<ref name="Easter eggs">{{SW|url=news/inside-ahsoka-easter-eggs-sabine-wren|text=Inside ''Ahsoka'': 12 Easter Eggs from Sabine Wren's Lothal Lookout}}</ref> Concept art for Wren's room was done by [[Matt Allsopp]], with concept art of Murley in the room done by [[Christian Alzmann]] in March [[2022]],<ref name="Ahsoka concept">{{SW|url=concept-art-ahsoka|text=Concept Art &#124; Ahsoka}}</ref> and a large physical set was created with ''Rebels'' and ''Ahsoka'' creator [[Dave Filoni]] and ''Ahsoka''{{'s}} production designers recreating various elements and nods to the animated series.<ref name="Easter eggs" />

